# Local benchmark output. The CLI writes these when run with --json, and the
# numbers are specific to the machine that produced them -- a run on a slow
# host reports a HIGHER score, because the load generator shares its CPU with
# the service and cannot apply full load. Committing them would put a figure
# in the repo that does not describe the service. Measured results belong in
# the README, sourced from the graded platform.
benchmark-report*.json
